[[!meta title="Version 2.03.44 - Feature and Bug Fix Release"]]

Version 2.03.44
===============

* **INCOMPATIBLE** `fsadm` no longer honors `_FSADM_YES` environment variable,
  use `--yes` on the command line.
* Improve metadata reading speeds - see `global/io_engine` configuration option. See [[!toggle text="more"]].
* Deprecate `global/use_aio` configuration option in favor of `global/io_engine`.
* Lot of small fixes in `dmeventd`, and fixes, modernization, and hardening of scripts mainly `lvresize_fs_helper`, `lvm_import_vdo`, `fsadm`, `lvmdump`, `blkdeactivate`.
* Detect NVMe multipath devices and handle uncached primary devices.
* Use the correct VDO pool data LV size for VDO memory checks.
* Warn about RAID reshape data corruption on kernels older than 6.11.
* Improvements in RAID handling.
* Few changes in shared locking.
* And [[!toggle text="more"]]

[[!toggleable text="""
Configurable I/O engine
-----------------------

User can now select from multiple I/O engines, depending on what's supported by the system.
This will help with metadata reading time especially on systems with heavy use of lvs.

* Deprecate use_aio. `use_aio=0` still selects sync I/O.
* By default all available engines with installed libraries are on, see configure options below.
* Default the I/O engine to iouring, then threads, then libaio, then sync.

Changes in command line
-----------------------

* Use `lvmdump -c` to return lvmlockd status instead of clvmd.
* Add `lvmdump -A` option to enable all collection options at once.

Improved RAID handling
----------------------

* Preserve RAID1 recovery state and rebuild markers when reducing images.
* Accept transient or incomplete dm-raid status during repair and reduction.
* Report the dead-primary RAID repair advice instead of refusing a rebuild.
* Run mirror repair from dmeventd when mirror reports in-sync with failed legs.
* Handle incomplete RAID health status from dm-raid 1.9.0/1.9.1.

Changes in shared locking
--------------------------

* Apply `lvmlockd --lockopt force` to all lock requests.
* Keep PR state after failed start - see lvmpersist(8) section *Errors durin PR start*.
* Allow vgextend before any host starts PR on new devs - see lvmpersist(8).
* Apply PTPL when extending VG to ensure persistence when power cycling devs.

./configure options
-------------------

* New `--with{,out}-{libaio,liburing}` options controlling available `io_engine` settings.

And more
--------

* Improve documentation about PVs layered on top of LVs.

"""]]

